Groundfighting is the art of maintaining combat effectiveness when knocked
prone or otherwise fighting from the ground. While most combatants suffer
severe penalties when not on their feet, those trained in groundfighting
can continue to defend themselves and even attack effectively.

This passive skill reduces the combat penalties normally associated with
fighting while prone. At maximum proficiency, groundfighting can eliminate
these penalties entirely, making the practitioner nearly as dangerous on
their back as they are standing.

Groundfighting is invaluable when facing opponents who use knockdown
attacks or in situations where maintaining footing is difficult. Rather
than scrambling to stand, a skilled groundfighter can continue the battle
from any position.

Class: Monk
Discipline: Leverage

